+# U-Boot environment location on the Anpviz/UVision N803 (OEM KL_LX510 U-Boot).
+#
+# Deliberately a FILE, not flash. Unlike the MC-A85/JL12D2 (whose OEM env
+# overlapped the kernel partition and bricked on fw_setenv), the N803 HAS a
+# dedicated ENV partition (mtd1, 0x4F000..0x50000), so writing real flash env
+# would be safe here. We still point fw_setenv/fw_printenv at a scratch file:
+# U-Boot auto-boots from its own env (bootcmd "sf read KERNEL; bootm") and the
+# thingino kernel forces its own command line, so nothing in Linux needs to
+# reach U-Boot's real env -- and a scratch file cannot touch flash at all. If a
+# future need arises to edit the real U-Boot env from Linux, repoint this at
+# "/dev/mtd1 0x0 0x1000 0x1000" (safe on this board; mtd1 is ENV-only).
+#
+# <device> <offset> <env size>
+/etc/fw_env.dat 0x0 0x10000
